    <statement><p>Find the area of the surface obtained by rotating the curve
<me>y = 2x^{3}</me>
from <m>x = 0</m> to <m>x = 1</m> about the <m>x</m>-axis.</p>
<p>The area is <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/> square units.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\pi }{27\cdot 2}\mathopen{}\left(\left(1+9\cdot 2\cdot 2\cdot 1^{4}\right)^{1.5}-1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
